      "writtenOn": "2024-02-28T15:07:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need the fix presented in this CL for a case where the peer is sink and we are using the new AVRCP profile implementation. I found in the code such ways to distinguish the new and the old one:\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/bta/av/bta_av_aact.cc;drc\u003d7881793e9b56994212d3a7c31795bec682c53c4d;l\u003d3064\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/bta/av/bta_av_aact.cc;drc\u003d7881793e9b56994212d3a7c31795bec682c53c4d;l\u003d3078\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/bta/av/bta_av_act.cc;drc\u003d49ac8b74a83c293e8c3097691f1781d20ad80aad;l\u003d335\n\nNow the legacy AVRCP has that fix implemented already here:\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/btif/src/btif_av.cc;drc\u003d49ac8b74a83c293e8c3097691f1781d20ad80aad;l\u003d1767\n\nSo I wanted to invoke it from the new implementation, which does not rely on btif_rc_(...), and omit the check btif_rc_is_connected_peer() as it would always fail in this case. \n\nThis ensures that we don\u0027t break the old version and we fix the new implementation.\n\nIf you know about a better way of determining which AVRCP implementation is being used please let me know, as I did struggle with that ; )",
      "parentUuid": "8795fc90_95af54e9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2867,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 2867,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "e3bc1c41518a06824aa43870709ef427d2464eca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4dabeddd_ba3ecf4f",
        "filename": "system/btif/src/btif_av.cc",
